  "_comment": "Room backdrops: a fill colour plus parallax layers, far → near. Every layer key is required: texture, factor (0 = glued to the camera, 1 = glued to the world), tint, repeat_x, repeat_y, y_px (offset in art px), scale (draw magnification — the SSW packs are 32 px/tile-era art, so 1 at our 32 px tiles). 'greybox' must stay layer-less. Tuning rules (reviewed 2026-10-13 against the real image sizes): far layers 0.1–0.3, near 0.5–0.7; y_px puts a layer's silhouette top in the upper third of a 540 px view with the camera at the room top; repeat_y only for sheets that actually tile vertically (the SET3/SET4 cave fills) — the silhouette cutouts (SSWorlds_SET2, SET5, CastlePack, SET7, SSW2_SET2) do not; where a cutout stack has no opaque sky under it, color is the bottom-row colour of the nearest cutout so its lower edge blends when the camera scrolls past it. SSW_SET4_MainBackTile.png is a 32 px back-wall TILE SHEET (paint it in DecorBack), not a parallax texture. Sources: assets/backdrops/SOURCES.md.",
